        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve: polish agent workspace cron panels",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Agents workspace Files and Cron Jobs panels were technically functional but visually disconnected. Operators had to switch between instruction files and scheduled jobs without a clear workspace summary, per-agent schedule summary, or dense scan-friendly job cards.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis refresh keeps the existing Agents tab structure and gateway contracts, but upgrades the Files and Cron Jobs panels in place. Files now show workspace/file metadata and clearer file cards, while Cron Jobs now show per-agent schedule metrics and richer job cards with schedule, target, state, payload, and Run Now controls.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can inspect an agent workspace and its recurring work faster from the Agents screen. The UI now makes selected files, missing files, enabled jobs, next wake, next agent run, and each job payload easier to scan without adding new backend state or navigation concepts.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/ui/views/agents.test.ts`\n- `pnpm format:check -- ui/src/ui/views/agents-panels-status-files.ts ui/src/ui/views/agents.test.ts ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts ui/src/styles/components.css`\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:check`\n- `pnpm tsgo:test:ui`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --parallel-tests \"node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/ui/views/agents.test.ts\"` clean: no accepted/actionable findings\n\nVisual screenshot not included: the mock Control UI server has workspace file fixtures but no cron method fixtures, so it would not prove the Cron panel meaningfully.\n",
